\title{The Subtraction Rule}
\date{2026-04-29T11:08:31Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Principle}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{If choosing something means making one choice in #{c_1} ways OR another in #{c_2} ways, but \em{the choices overlap}, the total number of choices is #{c_1 + c_2 - (\text{the number of choices in common})}.}

\p{Another way to write this, which we have seen before, is ##{|A \cup B| = |A| + |B| - |A \cap B|.}}

